# Repo-wide EOL policy. Without this, EOL handling depends on each developer's
# local core.autocrlf; the Windows Git installer default (autocrlf=true) checks
# every text file out as CRLF, which would break byte-exact / hash-of-source
# assertions and reintroduce CRLF churn. Normalize all text to LF in the repo
# and check it out as LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Source files are always text: force a text diff even if a blob accidentally
# contains a NUL byte. Otherwise git renders "Binary files differ" and hides the
# change from review — the exact hazard the NUL-byte escaping addressed (a
# converted file whose pre-image still held a NUL showed no reviewable hunk).
*.ts   diff
*.tsx  diff
*.mts  diff
*.cts  diff
*.js   diff
*.mjs  diff
*.cjs  diff

# Binary assets: never normalize or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.node binary
*.wasm binary
